WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.299
Coding Exercise 2 asks for one row per diagnosis
with an admission count The

00:00:06.326 --> 00:00:11.486
phrase one row per diagnosis tells you the GROUP BY
grain Add

00:00:11.512 --> 00:00:15.525
the aggregate count group by diagnosis and sort so
the largest count

00:00:15.552 --> 00:00:22.257
appears first Use Run and Check when you are ready
After

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:27.286
the query runs inspect the first row Ask whether the
diagnosis with

00:00:27.299 --> 00:00:32.274
the largest number of admissions is at the top If
your result

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.287
has one row per admission instead of one row per
diagnosis revisit

00:00:36.313 --> 00:00:41.777
the grouping If PostgreSQL reports a grouping error
check whether every selected

00:00:41.803 --> 00:00:47.515
non-aggregate column is represented correctly The
goal is to connect the written

00:00:47.542 --> 00:00:49.844
requirement directly to the GROUP BY list
